    {
      "id": "SDM-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-short-detector-absorption",
      "title": "The coefficient-square constant and uniform absorption in the selected windows",
      "hypotheses": "Positive integer U,J; Möbius product with cutoffs Y,N. For each character in S, the selected block has absolute value at least 1/(2J). For the uniform zero-detection windows Q is at least a fixed Q₀≥20 depending only on C.",
      "statement": "With e=1/400, A=max(1,1/(e log 2)), K=ceil(2^(1/e)), C=A^(2K), the coefficient sum of squares is ≤C U^(−197/200). If 8CQ³ U^(−197/200) ≤ 1/(8J²), then |S| ≤8CJ²U^(3/200). The selected windows attain that condition simultaneously for large enough Q.",
      "definitions": [
        "b(n)=a(n)n^(−399/400); X=ceil Q,Y=X⁴,J=8(floor(log₂X)+1),N=2^J and U=Y2^j for 0≤j<J."
      ],
